---
import AdminLayout from '../../layouts/AdminLayout.astro';
import pkg from '../../../package.json';

const user = Astro.locals.user;

// Role gate: only admin or superadmin may access
if (!user || (user.role !== 'admin' && user.role !== 'superadmin')) {
    return Astro.redirect('/admin', 302);
}

const lastUpdated = 'July 2026';
---

<AdminLayout title="System Documentation">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto">
        <div class="mb-10 border-b border-border pb-6">
            <h2 class="text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-foreground uppercase">System Documentation</h2>
            <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground mt-3 font-medium max-w-3xl">
                Read this documentation and the source code to understand the system design.
            </p>
            <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-3">WARITAKU CMS v{pkg.version} &mdash; Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-8">
            <div class="lg:col-span-3 space-y-12">
                
                {/* 0. Critical System Rules & Database Environments */}
                <section id="docs-environments" class="bg-card border border-border rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm relative overflow-hidden group hover:border-red-500/50 transition-colors scroll-mt-24">
                    <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-1.5 h-full bg-red-500/80 group-hover:bg-red-500 transition-colors"></div>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-black mb-4 border-b border-border/50 pb-3 uppercase tracking-wider text-red-500">Database Environments & Safety</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-4 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed text-sm">
                        
                        <div class="bg-destructive/10 border-l-4 border-destructive p-4 rounded-r-md">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-destructive mb-1">CRITICAL SYSTEM RULE: Database Preservation</h4>
                            <p class="text-sm text-destructive/90 mb-3">
                                <strong>Do not delete or recreate the database folder (`.wrangler`).</strong> 
                                The local database copies the production database. If you delete it, you lose synchronized data. 
                                AI agents must not run deletion commands or add dummy data unless the user types: "Purge Development Database".
                            </p>
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-destructive mb-1">CRITICAL SYSTEM RULE: Database Migrations</h4>
                            <p class="text-sm text-destructive/90">
                                <strong>Never run <code>wrangler d1 migrations apply --local</code> blindly.</strong> 
                                If the <code>d1_migrations</code> table is empty or missing (e.g., if tables were created manually or via <code>drizzle-kit push</code>), Wrangler may forcefully wipe and recreate the local SQLite file from scratch to apply migrations, resulting in total data loss. Always verify the migration state before running apply.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="bg-muted/30 p-4 rounded-md border border-border mt-4">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-foreground mb-2">Environments</h4>
                            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
                                <li>
                                    <strong class="text-foreground">Local Development:</strong> Uses Miniflare. The system stores SQLite files at: 
                                    <code class="px-1 py-0.5 bg-background rounded border text-xs break-all">.wrangler/state/v3/d1/miniflare-D1DatabaseObject/</code>. 
                                    This database is isolated. Connect using `npm run dev` or local D1 commands such as <code class="px-1 py-0.5 bg-background rounded text-xs">npx wrangler d1 execute DB --local --command="..."</code>.
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <strong class="text-foreground">Local Cloud Development (Preview):</strong> Uses a remote Cloudflare D1 database for testing. Connect using the `--remote` flag: <code class="px-1 py-0.5 bg-background rounded text-xs">npm run dev --remote</code>.
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <strong class="text-foreground">Production:</strong> The main database on the Cloudflare edge network. Access it through deployed code or explicit `--remote` D1 commands.
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                        <div class="bg-muted/30 p-4 rounded-md border border-border mt-4">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-foreground mb-2">Adapter Pattern</h4>
                            <p class="mb-3">Waritaku CMS uses modular architecture. The core engine uses Cloudflare D1 Database and R2 Storage for fast performance.</p>
                            <p class="mb-3">The system uses the Generic Adapter Pattern. To deploy on other infrastructure (such as Vercel, Netlify, or AWS), modify two files:</p>
                            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
                                <li>
                                    <strong class="text-foreground">Database Adapter (<code>src/lib/db.ts</code>)</strong>: 
                                    All components and API routes import the database connection from `getDb(env)`. To use PostgreSQL, update the Drizzle logic in this file.
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <strong class="text-foreground">Storage Adapter (<code>src/lib/storage.ts</code>)</strong>: 
                                    Media operations use `StorageAdapter` methods (`uploadFile`, `deleteFile`, `listFiles`). To use AWS S3, update these methods with the AWS SDK.
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                        <div class="bg-muted/30 p-4 rounded-md border border-border mt-4 space-y-3">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-foreground mb-2">Directory Structure & Uploads</h4>
                            <p>Project folder structure:</p>
                            <pre class="bg-card p-4 rounded-lg border border-border text-xs overflow-x-auto text-foreground font-mono">
waritaku/
├── public/                 # Static assets served at root URL /
├── local_uploads/          # Local media storage (development mode only)
├── src/
│   ├── assets/             # Raw image and icon assets
│   ├── components/         # React and Astro UI components
│   │   └── editor/         # TipTap WYSIWYG editor components
│   ├── db/                 # Drizzle ORM schema definitions and migrations
│   ├── i18n/               # Internationalization strings and translation keys
│   ├── layouts/            # Page layouts (AdminLayout, Layout, etc.)
│   ├── lib/                # Database (db.ts) and Storage (storage.ts) adapters
│   ├── middleware.ts       # Authentication, redirect checks, and 404 logging
│   ├── pages/              # Routing endpoints and public page layouts
│   │   ├── admin/          # Admin CMS management pages and documentation
│   │   └── api/            # API endpoints (media, tags, exports, etc.)
│   ├── styles/             # Global CSS definitions and Tailwind setup
│   └── utils/              # Helper utilities and text parsing functions
├── .wrangler/              # Miniflare local D1 database state (do not commit)
├── astro.config.mjs        # Astro configuration and Vite plugins
├── drizzle.config.ts       # Drizzle ORM configuration
└── package.json            # Dependencies and scripts
                            </pre>
                            <p>Directory functions:</p>
                            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-3">
                                <li><strong><code>/src</code></strong>: Contains Astro pages, React components, Drizzle DB schema (`src/db`), and layouts.</li>
                                <li><strong><code>/public</code></strong>: Contains static assets. The server serves these files at the root URL `/`.</li>
                                <li><strong><code>/.wrangler</code></strong>: Miniflare creates this folder. It contains the local D1 database. Do not commit this folder to Git.</li>
                                <li class="bg-card/50 p-3 rounded border border-border/50">
                                    <strong class="text-primary text-[15px]">The <code>/local_uploads</code> Directory</strong>
                                    <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">Stores uploaded media during local development.</p>
                                    
                                    <strong class="block mt-3 text-foreground">Local operation:</strong> 
                                    <p class="mt-1">When you upload an image during `npm run dev`, the system writes the file to <code>/local_uploads</code>. A custom Vite plugin (`serve-local-uploads` in <code>astro.config.mjs</code>) serves files from this folder for requests to <code>/uploads/*</code>.</p>
                                    
                                    <strong class="block mt-3 text-foreground">Production operation:</strong> 
                                    <p class="mt-1">In production, the server detects the <code>env.UPLOADS</code> R2 binding. The system uploads media to Cloudflare R2 and ignores the local folder. Do not commit <code>/local_uploads</code> to Git.</p>
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                {/* 1. Dashboard */}
                <section id="docs-dashboard" class="bg-card border border-border rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm relative overflow-hidden group hover:border-primary/50 transition-colors scroll-mt-24">
                    <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-1.5 h-full bg-primary/80 group-hover:bg-primary transition-colors"></div>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-black mb-4 border-b border-border/50 pb-3 uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Overview: Dashboard</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-4 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed text-sm">
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Function:</strong> Shows real-time summary statistics, interactive publishing calendar, day-of-week productivity analytics, and recent content activity table.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Database Query:</strong> Executes aggregated queries dynamically based on `collections`, querying the `entries` and `users` tables via Drizzle ORM.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Technology:</strong> Astro SSR for server processing, React components for interactive calendar &amp; analytics, Tailwind CSS for layout.</p>
                        <div class="bg-muted/30 p-4 rounded-md border border-border mt-4">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-foreground mb-2">Dashboard Toolkit (Customization)</h4>
                            <p class="mb-2">Superadmin users can toggle, reorder, and configure individual dashboard widgets under <a href="/admin/layout/dashboard" class="text-primary hover:underline font-semibold">Appearance &rarr; Dashboard Layout</a>.</p>
                            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                                <li><strong class="text-foreground">Summary Cards:</strong> Overview metrics dynamically loaded for configured Collections (like Articles and Pages), Taxonomies, and Users.</li>
                                <li><strong class="text-foreground">Publishing Calendar:</strong> Monthly view of published entries and publishing productivity breakdown.</li>
                                <li><strong class="text-foreground">Recent Activity:</strong> Detailed feed of latest published and draft entries across all collections.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section id="docs-collections-entries" class="bg-card border border-border rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm relative overflow-hidden group hover:border-blue-500/50 transition-colors scroll-mt-24">
                    <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-1.5 h-full bg-blue-500/80 group-hover:bg-blue-500 transition-colors"></div>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-black mb-4 border-b border-border/50 pb-3 uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-500">Content Types: Collections &amp; Entries</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-4 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed text-sm">
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Function:</strong> Defines content architecture dynamically and manages content items.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Database Structure:</strong>
                            - <strong>`collections`</strong>: Stores JSON schemas defining custom fields, taxonomy requirements, and block builder configurations.
                            - <strong>`entries`</strong>: Stores the actual content. Specific fields are stored in a flexible JSON `data` column, linking back to `collections.id`.
                            - <strong>`entry_revisions`</strong>: Stores version snapshots of entries for rollback capabilities.
                        </p>
                        
                        <div class="bg-blue-500/10 border-l-4 border-blue-500 p-4 mt-4 rounded-r-md">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 mb-2">Baked-in Examples: Articles &amp; Pages</h4>
                            <p class="text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 mb-2">While the system is fully dynamic, it comes pre-baked with two primary collections as examples:</p>
                            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300">
                                <li><strong>Articles:</strong> Represents blog posts or news items. Built to utilize Taxonomies (like Categories and Tags) and heavily focuses on TipTap rich-text content for the main body.</li>
                                <li><strong>Pages:</strong> Represents static or modular routes (like About Us, Contact, or Custom 404 Pages). Pages extensively utilize the <strong>Block Builder</strong> to drag-and-drop structural components (Hero sections, grids, lists) rather than just linear text.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                        <div class="bg-muted/30 p-4 rounded-md border border-border mt-4 space-y-3">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-foreground mb-2">Dynamic Entry Editor</h4>
                            <p>The `DynamicEntryEditor.tsx` component reads the collection schema and automatically renders the appropriate editing experience:</p>
                            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
                                <li><strong>TipTap Editor:</strong> Rich text editing with Image controls (alignment, captions), FAQ shortcodes, and JSON-LD overrides.</li>
                                <li><strong>Block Builder:</strong> Modular design system for assembling pages using dynamic components (e.g., Article Grids filtered by Taxonomies).</li>
                                <li><strong>Revision Control:</strong> Full snapshot history is preserved for every entry across all collections, allowing seamless restoration via the <em>Revisions</em> toolbar button.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                {/* 4. My Profile */}
                <section id="docs-profile" class="bg-card border border-border rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm relative overflow-hidden group hover:border-purple-500/50 transition-colors scroll-mt-24">
                    <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-1.5 h-full bg-purple-500/80 group-hover:bg-purple-500 transition-colors"></div>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-black mb-4 border-b border-border/50 pb-3 uppercase tracking-wider text-purple-500">Content: My Profile</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-4 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed text-sm">
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Function:</strong> Allows users to update profile details, passwords, and social links.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Database Structure:</strong> Updates the `users` table. The `socialLinks` column stores JSON string data.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Technology:</strong> Uses `bcrypt` to hash passwords before database storage.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Editable Fields:</strong> Email, password, names, display name, author slug, avatar URL, biography, and social links.</p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                {/* 5. Taxonomies & Terms */}
                <section id="docs-taxonomies-terms" class="bg-card border border-border rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm relative overflow-hidden group hover:border-amber-500/50 transition-colors scroll-mt-24">
                    <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-1.5 h-full bg-amber-500/80 group-hover:bg-amber-500 transition-colors"></div>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-black mb-4 border-b border-border/50 pb-3 uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-500">Content: Taxonomies &amp; Terms</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-4 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed text-sm">
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Function:</strong> A generic classification system for grouping entries.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Database Structure:</strong> 
                            - <strong>`taxonomies`</strong>: Defines the classification group (e.g., 'Categories' or 'Tags'). It dictates if terms are hierarchical or flat.
                            - <strong>`terms`</strong>: The actual classification items (e.g., 'Technology', 'News').
                            - <strong>`entry_terms`</strong>: Join table linking `entries` to `terms`.
                        </p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Technology:</strong> Uses Astro form actions for CRUD operations. Drizzle ORM queries fetch filtered entries based on term slugs.</p>
                        
                        <div class="bg-amber-500/10 border-l-4 border-amber-500 p-4 mt-4 rounded-r-md">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 mb-1">Baked-in Examples: Categories &amp; Tags</h4>
                            <p class="text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-300">
                                Similar to Articles/Pages, the system comes with <strong>Categories</strong> (hierarchical, primary routing) and <strong>Tags</strong> (flat keywords) pre-baked into the `taxonomies` table to demonstrate how to structure entry groupings.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                {/* 7. Media Library */}
                <section id="docs-media" class="bg-card border border-border rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm relative overflow-hidden group hover:border-cyan-500/50 transition-colors scroll-mt-24">
                    <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-1.5 h-full bg-cyan-500/80 group-hover:bg-cyan-500 transition-colors"></div>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-black mb-4 border-b border-border/50 pb-3 uppercase tracking-wider text-cyan-500">Content: Media Library</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-4 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed text-sm">
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Function:</strong> Uploads and manages media files.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Database Structure:</strong> Files exist in object storage. Articles store file URL strings.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Technology:</strong> Cloudflare R2 bucket (`waritaku-uploads`). Vite middleware handles local requests.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">UI Display:</strong> Calls `env.UPLOADS.list()` to display files in a grid.</p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                {/* 8. Users & Roles */}
                <section id="docs-users" class="bg-card border border-border rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm relative overflow-hidden group hover:border-orange-500/50 transition-colors scroll-mt-24">
                    <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-1.5 h-full bg-orange-500/80 group-hover:bg-orange-500 transition-colors"></div>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-black mb-4 border-b border-border/50 pb-3 uppercase tracking-wider text-orange-500">System: Users & Roles</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-4 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed text-sm">
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Function:</strong> Manages user access and permission levels.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Database Structure:</strong> Updates the `users` table. The `articles` and `pages` tables reference `users.id` as `authorId`.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Technology:</strong> Astro middleware (`src/middleware.ts`) verifies session tokens against the `users` table for each request.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Permissions:</strong> Supports `admin` and `superadmin` roles. The UI hides administrative tools from users who lack the `superadmin` role.</p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                {/* 9. General Settings */}
                <section id="docs-general-settings" class="bg-card border border-border rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm relative overflow-hidden group hover:border-zinc-500/50 transition-colors scroll-mt-24">
                    <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-1.5 h-full bg-zinc-500/80 group-hover:bg-zinc-500 transition-colors"></div>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-black mb-4 border-b border-border/50 pb-3 uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-500">System: General Settings</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-4 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed text-sm">
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Function:</strong> Configures site title, tagline, logo, favicon, and custom HTML scripts. Only `superadmin` users can access this section.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Database Structure:</strong> Stores settings as a JSON object in the `settings` table under `general_settings`.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Technology:</strong> Uses React Hook Form to manage state before sending JSON to Astro endpoints.</p>
                        
                        <div class="bg-muted/30 p-4 rounded-md border border-border mt-4 space-y-3">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-foreground mb-2">Custom Script Locations</h4>
                            <p>You can add HTML or JavaScript to three layout zones:</p>
                            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                                <li>`headerHtml`: Injects content before <code>&lt;/head&gt;</code>.</li>
                                <li>`footerHtml`: Injects content before <code>&lt;/body&gt;</code>.</li>
                                <li>`articleBottomHtml`: Injects content after article text in `[slug].astro`.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                {/* 10. System Advanced */}
                <section id="docs-system-advanced" class="bg-card border border-border rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm relative overflow-hidden group hover:border-red-500/50 transition-colors scroll-mt-24">
                    <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-1.5 h-full bg-red-500/80 group-hover:bg-red-500 transition-colors"></div>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-black mb-4 border-b border-border/50 pb-3 uppercase tracking-wider text-red-500">System: Advanced System</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-4 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed text-sm">
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Function:</strong> Handles system exports, API key storage, and environment labels.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Database Structure:</strong> Reads and writes to the `settings` table (`system_secrets` and `database_environment`).</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Technology:</strong> `/api/export-db.ts` generates JSON database backups. Checks `env.UPLOADS` to report CDN status.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Security:</strong> Restricted to `superadmin` users. API keys remain on the server and do not enter client bundles.</p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                {/* 11. Redirections & 404 Engine */}
                <section id="docs-system-redirects" class="bg-card border border-border rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm relative overflow-hidden group hover:border-orange-500/50 transition-colors scroll-mt-24 mt-8">
                    <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-1.5 h-full bg-orange-500/80 group-hover:bg-orange-500 transition-colors"></div>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-black mb-4 border-b border-border/50 pb-3 uppercase tracking-wider text-orange-500">System: Redirections & 404 Engine</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-4 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed text-sm">
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Function:</strong> Logs 404 errors and processes 301 redirect rules.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Database Structure:</strong> Uses `redirects` (stores redirect rules) and `not_found_logs` (stores 404 URL logs).</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Technology:</strong> Astro Middleware (`src/middleware.ts`) checks URL paths on Cloudflare Workers.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Log Cleanup:</strong> When you add a redirect rule for a logged URL, the system deletes that URL from the 404 log.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Control:</strong> Disable redirects and 404 tracking in **General Settings -&gt; SEO & Edge Routing**.</p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                {/* 12. Navigation & Footer */}
                <section id="docs-navigation" class="bg-card border border-border rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm relative overflow-hidden group hover:border-indigo-500/50 transition-colors scroll-mt-24">
                    <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-1.5 h-full bg-indigo-500/80 group-hover:bg-indigo-500 transition-colors"></div>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-black mb-4 border-b border-border/50 pb-3 uppercase tracking-wider text-indigo-500">Appearance: Navigation & Footer</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-4 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed text-sm">
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Function:</strong> Configures menu links for the header and footer.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Database Structure:</strong> Stores links as a JSON array of `&#123;label, url, target&#125;` objects in the `settings` table.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Technology:</strong> React manages the admin menu editor interface.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Rendering:</strong> `src/layouts/LayoutGlobalHeader.astro` and `LayoutGlobalFooter.astro` render the menu links.</p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                {/* 13. Front Page Builder */}
                <section id="docs-frontpage" class="bg-card border border-border rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm relative overflow-hidden group hover:border-lime-500/50 transition-colors scroll-mt-24">
                    <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-1.5 h-full bg-lime-500/80 group-hover:bg-lime-500 transition-colors"></div>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-black mb-4 border-b border-border/50 pb-3 uppercase tracking-wider text-lime-500">Appearance: Front Page Builder</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-4 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed text-sm">
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Function:</strong> Configures section blocks on the front page.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Database Structure:</strong> Saves block configurations to `settings` under `frontpage_layout`.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Technology:</strong> `index.astro` reads block configurations and fetches article data with `Promise.all()` queries.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Rendering:</strong> Renders Astro components (such as `NewHeroType3.astro` and `CategoryBlock.astro`) based on configured block types.</p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                {/* 13. Global Sidebar */}
                <section id="docs-sidebar" class="bg-card border border-border rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm relative overflow-hidden group hover:border-fuchsia-500/50 transition-colors scroll-mt-24">
                    <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-1.5 h-full bg-fuchsia-500/80 group-hover:bg-fuchsia-500 transition-colors"></div>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-black mb-4 border-b border-border/50 pb-3 uppercase tracking-wider text-fuchsia-500">Appearance: Global Sidebar</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-4 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed text-sm">
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Function:</strong> Configures widgets in the sidebar of article and category pages.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Database Structure:</strong> Stores widget configurations as a JSON array in `settings` under `sidebar_widgets`.</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Technology:</strong> React manages admin settings (`SidebarSettings.tsx`). Astro renders the sidebar (`sidebar.astro`).</p>
                        <p><strong class="text-foreground">Widgets:</strong> Supports search, recent posts, and custom HTML widgets.</p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                {/* 14. Theme Colors */}
