                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-black mb-4 border-b border-border/50 pb-3 uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">WordPress Migration</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-6 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed text-sm">

                        <div class="bg-muted/30 p-4 rounded-md border border-border">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-foreground mb-2">What the pipeline does</h4>
                            <p>Two scripts handle a full WordPress → Waritaku CMS migration:</p>
                            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1">
                                <li><code class="px-1 py-0.5 bg-background rounded border text-xs">scripts/wp-import.mjs</code> — Parses the WordPress MySQL dump (.sql). Extracts users, categories, tags, articles, pages, SEO meta. Rewrites <code class="px-1 py-0.5 bg-background rounded border text-xs">wp-content/uploads</code> URLs to <code class="px-1 py-0.5 bg-background rounded border text-xs">/uploads/</code>. Converts shortcodes. Outputs <code class="px-1 py-0.5 bg-background rounded border text-xs">import_payload.json</code> and <code class="px-1 py-0.5 bg-background rounded border text-xs">migration_report.json</code>.</li>
                                <li><code class="px-1 py-0.5 bg-background rounded border text-xs">scripts/wp-import-images.mjs</code> — Copies original images from the WordPress uploads directory to <code class="px-1 py-0.5 bg-background rounded border text-xs">local_uploads/</code>, skipping all WordPress-generated derived files.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

