                            <h4 class="font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Step-by-step workflow (Live or Dead/Archived Site)</h4>
                            <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-3">
                                <li>
                                    <strong class="text-foreground">Prepare your folder structure</strong><br/>
                                    Place your project and the old WordPress export (MySQL .sql dump + uploads) in sibling directories:
                                    <pre class="mt-1 text-xs bg-background border border-border rounded p-2 overflow-x-auto">antigravity/
  waritaku/                 ← this CMS
  waritaku.old/
    public_html/
      wp-content/
        uploads/            ← images
    dump.sql                ← MySQL dump</pre>
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <strong class="text-foreground">Run the SQL parser (handles Live or Dead sites)</strong>
                                    <pre class="mt-1 text-xs bg-background border border-border rounded p-2"># Standard auto-detection (reads siteurl from wp_options &amp; auto-scans all upload domains)
node scripts/wp-import.mjs dump.sql

# For dead/archived sites with custom old domains:
node scripts/wp-import.mjs dump.sql --old-domain oldsite.com,fuyukaiblog.files.wordpress.com</pre>
                                    Auto-scans the dump for ALL domain names used in upload URLs and rewrites them into local <code class="px-1 py-0.5 bg-background rounded border text-xs">/uploads/</code> paths.
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <strong class="text-foreground">Copy images</strong>
                                    <pre class="mt-1 text-xs bg-background border border-border rounded p-2"># Copy originals as-is (fast, ~80s for 65k images)
node scripts/wp-import-images.mjs

# OR convert to WebP for 50% smaller storage (~30min)
node scripts/wp-import-images.mjs --clean --webp</pre>
                                    Always use <code class="px-1 py-0.5 bg-background rounded border text-xs">--clean</code> when switching modes to avoid duplicate .jpg + .webp files.
                                </li>
                                <li>
